      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Perhaps a good solution to this problem is a kind of invite approval/proxy system.\n\nI am the instance owner.\nCasuallynoted is also in the instance with me.\nCasuallynoted is friends with VRPill but I am not.\nCasuallynoted tries to send VRPill an invite, this gets proxied through me.\nI see a notification saying that Casuallynoted would like approval to invite his friend, VRPill.\nI have options to accept, decline, etc.\nI accept and VRPill gets an invite from me saying \"On behalf of Casuallynoted, come join us!\" or whatever.\n\nI believe a process like this would solve the problem along with preventing the ability to just search up any random user and send them an invite. With this they understand who actually wants them to come along.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
