  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-11T17:22:54.129Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Everyone knows the grief of trying to organize a group together and your friends want you to invite their friends who want you to invite their friends and so on and so forth. Usually this results in the room  owner mass-friending people who they don't really know and may not ever become close with. Why do we need to be friends with someone to invite them to an instance? I think it would be neat to be able to just search someone up and invite them in regardless of their friends status- relegating friends only to who can request invites and/or join off of a friends-only instance. This would just remove an extra, and oftentimes unnecessary step.",
